      "sourceTextSha256": "034cddd0f1c96f70228855939d55de04514d9956ae3f7373b07631b6621d3dec",
      "text": "Day 3 · Morning departure from Salta and transfer to Purmamarca (approx. 4 hours), for an excursion through the Quebrada de Humahuaca, a UNESCO World Heritage Site for its magnificent landscapes and a history going back more than 10,000 years, where indigenous fortresses, prehistoric caves, hamlets and pre-Columbian and colonial settlements are still preserved today.\n\nFrom Purmamarca, admire the Hill of Seven Colours and the old Church of Santa Rosa de Lima. The route continues to Tilcara and its ancient indigenous fortress, then past Uquía, whose church preserves one of the most important collections of the famous arquebusier angels. Visit Humahuaca, on the banks of the Río Grande, and stroll its narrow cobbled streets among colonial monuments.",
